<article class="env-lemma" id="0AFI">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AFI">Lemma <span data-tag="0AFI">67.37.10</span>.</a> Let $X$ and $Y$ be locally Noetherian algebraic spaces over a scheme $S$, and let $f : X \to Y$ be a smooth morphism. For every point $x \in |X|$ with image $y \in |Y|$, </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \dim _ x(X) = \dim _ y(Y) + \dim _ x(X_ y)  \]
</div>
  <p> where $\dim _ x(X_ y)$ is the relative dimension of $f$ at $x$ as in Definition <a href="/tag/04NM" data-tag="04NM">67.33.1</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By definition of the dimension of an algebraic space at a point (Properties of Spaces, Definition <a href="/tag/04N5" data-tag="04N5">66.9.1</a>), this reduces to the corresponding statement for schemes (Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/0AFF" data-tag="0AFF">29.35.21</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>